# Prose under its own scope
// <- meta.prose.lavin markup.heading.markdown punctuation.definition.heading.markdown
//^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ meta.prose.lavin entity.name.section.markdown

Every kind of Markdown in a literate file is prose, under meta.prose.lavin, and the program is not.
// <----- meta.prose.lavin -meta.embedded

    main() = 0
// <---------- meta.embedded.block.avin source.avin -meta.prose

Plain *emphasis*, **strong**, ~~struck~~ and `code` words.
// <---- meta.prose.lavin
//    ^^^^^^^^^^ meta.prose.lavin markup.italic.markdown
//                ^^^^^^^^^^ meta.prose.lavin markup.bold.markdown
//                            ^^^^^^^^^^ meta.prose.lavin markup.strikethrough.markdown
//                                           ^^^^^^ meta.prose.lavin markup.inline.raw.string.markdown

A [link](https://avin.dev "Avin"), an ![image](pic.png) and <https://avin.dev/x>.
// ^^^^ meta.prose.lavin meta.link.inline.markdown string.other.link.title.markdown
//       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ meta.prose.lavin markup.underline.link.markdown
//                                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ meta.prose.lavin meta.image.inline.markdown
//                                                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ meta.prose.lavin markup.underline.link.markdown

## A heading directly above the program
// <-- meta.prose.lavin markup.heading.markdown
    headed() = 1
// <------------ meta.embedded.block.avin -meta.prose -markup.heading

> A quoted line with `code`
